{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for E9 exact head 79fe78cfe2ef709a5352f537f0552f7d38f6d437; all 74 submitted artifacts covered. Both 7040317d findings are fixed: owner v3 retains every interrupted installer in pending and decodes the old v2 installing slot, and occupied live/foreign/partial recovery locks now wait and reach a named bounded error without removing the lock. The four previous independent failure-path probes now pass.\n\n[P2] Preserve the cleanup duty when a pending installation's file is unmarked. packages/cli/src/main.ts applyLocal release-lane, lines 340–358, prints a Manual local step for marker === null, then unconditionally filters that installation out of pending (and removes installed if owned). Reproduction uses actual CLI + real local Git + fake Room: workspace writes Y's credential, then saving its Room mapping fails; Y is only in owner.pending. Remove the first ownership-comment line, preserving the valid Git credential. Release Y succeeds, prints the manual instruction and leaves the credential, but deletes pending Y; the Room config never had a mapping, and the completed journal no longer retains the duty. This loses the only persistent cleanup evidence without proof that the credential was removed or replaced. Keep the owned installed/pending entries for an unmarked file, or transfer them to a persistent manual duty. Cancel the reservation independently. Settle evidence only for removal, absence, or proved replacement; test unmapped pending and installed cases, interruption/retry, and successor preservation. Independent fifth probe /tmp/artroom-checker-E9-diagnostics/checker-v9-review.test.ts confirms the lost-duty behavior.\n\nValidation: fresh npm ci --ignore-scripts (362 packages); complete workspace typecheck passes; Client 86 Node + 2 workerd, CLI 98, MCP 66 Node + 1 workerd tests pass; 5 independent probes pass (four controls proving fixes and one defect reproduction). CLI production bundle 954.0 KiB, real launcher --help works; local MCP Worker helper bundle 608.2 KiB passes, not a deployed endpoint. All four packages pack successfully; CLI archive includes bin/artroom.js. 68 submitted files are byte-identical to fully reviewed E8. Five changed/new text files read in full; lockfile parsed completely: 39 added records exactly match records already present in E8/approved main, one Git workspace record adopts main's Log test dependency, no removed records or changed metadata. All 131 inherited non-E changed files are byte-identical to approved main ad19956b. Coverage /tmp/artroom-checker-E9-byte-credit.json. Own diagnostic removed; detached worktree clean.\n\nArchitecture: plural unsettled evidence and reservation fencing correctly keep identity separate from file replacement; no elapsed-time proof of process death. The remaining duty should use the same evidence rule already applied to mapped manual cleanup, rather than a second forgetful path. Security: installation IDs fence deletion, credentials stay out of process arguments/transcripts, older or foreign locks require manual action, and release must not discard evidence merely because ownership is unreadable. Simplification: retaining a party until a marked replacement or absence is enough; no extra parallel credential registry is needed. Docs should describe the current record as v3 pending in the older review table as well.\n\nScope: this is an SDK/CLI/local MCP delivery review. Real Room-served MCP request 8ae3b2dca13fd9308a1247b27daef632fbc54df0, live deployment/auth/resource/whole-Room memory checks and full amendment runtime obligations remain required. No schedule estimate narrows them; fake Room and local helper bundling do not establish that deployed integration.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d6b3dd46e1c29541f6fb3717e68b61e560f72ea8","binding":"assigned","head":"79fe78cfe2ef709a5352f537f0552f7d38f6d437","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375e